From: pocket-debs
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 01:19:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] omacam-libcamera: NV12 frames converted to XRGB8888
Description:
 The app asks the camera for XRGB8888 and stops with "unsupported pixel
 format" when the configuration comes back with another format. A pipeline
 whose ISP writes YUV only, such as libcamera's simple pipeline with the
 MediaTek DIP as debayer, adjusts the stream to NV12.
 .
 Take NV12 as well: each frame is copied out of its buffer (both display
 modes then copy) and converted to XRGB8888 on up to four threads, with
 BT.601 or BT.709 coefficients and full or limited range from the stream's
 colour space (BT.601 full range where it names none). The rest of the app
 keeps seeing XRGB8888. Unit tests for the conversion.
Forwarded: no
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-21
